Trim the node to one outgoing channel first (docs/studies.md, study 2):

  sudo ./bench/use-arm.sh pin-cfg-@RELAY@                      # allowlist FIRST
  sudo -E ./tools/close-channels.py --keep @RELAY@ --send      # initiate closes
  sudo -E ./tools/close-channels.py --finalize --send          # after the grace period
  sudo ./bench/use-arm.sh pin-cfg-@RELAY@ --count              # must read 1

The allowlist only stops NEW channels being opened; it closes nothing. Without it
in place, the strategy would reopen what you close.
